{"t": 1794118159.4224007, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found, fix ready*\n\n*Cause:* the upstream ledger release 2026.11 added a `currency` field to every row. `reports/export.py` writes CSV with `csv.DictWriter(fieldnames=[\"id\",\"amount\"])`, which raises `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` on every export, so the API 502s at the gateway. CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1) shows ~4,120 occurrences of that error; reproduced locally.\n\n*Fix:* `export.py` now exports `id,amount,currency` and uses `extrasaction=\"ignore\"` so a future upstream field addition can't take the API down again. Verified: rows with/without `currency` and with unknown extra fields all export cleanly.\n\n*Action:* needs a deploy of reports-api (ECS, eu-west-1) to take effect \u2014 not yet deployed from here.\n\n*Heads-up:* the CSV gains a `currency` column at the end. Header-based consumers are fine; any consumer parsing the export by column position needs a look. No schema/consumer spec was findable (repo, docs, tickets), so the column is appended rather than reordered."}, "ok": true}
